{"id":"mahabharata-1-203","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":203,"title":"त्र्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 203 · The creation of Tilottama","summary":{"en":"The gods and sages appeal to Brahma, who has Vishvakarman fashion Tilottama, a woman of matchless beauty made from the best of every jewel. As she circles the assembly, Shiva grows four faces and Indra a thousand eyes to watch her, and Brahma sends her to the demons.","kn":"ದೇವತೆಗಳೂ ಋಷಿಗಳೂ ಬ್ರಹ್ಮನಲ್ಲಿ ಮೊರೆಯಿಡುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಅವನು ವಿಶ್ವಕರ್ಮನಿಂದ ಎಲ್ಲ ರತ್ನಗಳ ಶ್ರೇಷ್ಠಾಂಶದಿಂದ ಅಪ್ರತಿಮ ಸುಂದರಿ ತಿಲೋತ್ತಮೆಯನ್ನು ನಿರ್ಮಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅವಳು ಸಭೆಯನ್ನು ಪ್ರದಕ್ಷಿಣೆ ಮಾಡುವಾಗ ಅವಳನ್ನು ನೋಡಲು ಶಿವನಿಗೆ ನಾಲ್ಕು ಮುಖಗಳೂ ಇಂದ್ರನಿಗೆ ಸಾವಿರ ಕಣ್ಣುಗಳೂ ಮೂಡುತ್ತವೆ; ಬ್ರಹ್ಮನು ಅವಳನ್ನು ದೈತ್ಯರಲ್ಲಿಗೆ ಕಳುಹಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"देवता और ऋषि ब्रह्मा से प्रार्थना करते हैं, जो विश्वकर्मा से हर रत्न के श्रेष्ठ अंश से अनुपम सुन्दरी तिलोत्तमा बनवाते हैं। जब वह सभा की परिक्रमा करती है, उसे देखने के लिए शिव के चार मुख और इन्द्र के हज़ार नेत्र हो जाते हैं, और ब्रह्मा उसे दैत्यों के पास भेजते हैं।","te":"దేవతలు, ఋషులు బ్రహ్మను వేడుకోగా ఆయన విశ్వకర్మ చేత అన్ని రత్నాల శ్రేష్ఠాంశంతో అప్రతిమ సుందరి తిలోత్తమను సృష్టింపజేస్తాడు. ఆమె సభకు ప్రదక్షిణ చేస్తుండగా ఆమెను చూడడానికి శివునికి నాలుగు ముఖాలు, ఇంద్రునికి వెయ్యి కన్నులు కలుగుతాయి; బ్రహ్మ ఆమెను దైత్యుల వద్దకు పంపుతాడు.","ta":"தேவர்களும் முனிவர்களும் ப்ரஹ்மாவிடம் முறையிட, அவர் விஶ்வகர்மாவைக் கொண்டு ஒவ்வொரு ரத்தினத்தின் சிறந்த பகுதியால் ஒப்பற்ற அழகி திலோத்தமையைப் படைக்கிறார். அவள் சபையை வலம் வரும்போது அவளைக் காண ஶிவனுக்கு நான்கு முகங்களும் இந்திரனுக்கு ஆயிரம் கண்களும் தோன்றுகின்றன; ப்ரஹ்மா அவளை அசுரர்களிடம் அனுப்புகிறார்.","ml":"ദേവന്മാരും ഋഷിമാരും ബ്രഹ്മാവിനെ സമീപിക്കുന്നു; അദ്ദേഹം വിശ്വകർമ്മാവിനെക്കൊണ്ട്, ഓരോ രത്നത്തിലെയും ഏറ്റവും മികച്ചത് ചേർത്ത്, അതുല്യസൗന്ദര്യമുള്ള തിലോത്തമയെ സൃഷ്ടിക്കുന്നു. അവൾ സദസ്സിനെ വലംവെക്കുമ്പോൾ, അവളെ കാണാൻ ശിവന് നാലു മുഖങ്ങളും ഇന്ദ്രന് ആയിരം കണ്ണുകളും ഉണ്ടാകുന്നു; ബ്രഹ്മാവ് അവളെ അസുരന്മാരുടെ അടുത്തേക്ക് അയയ്ക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.203; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"अर्जुनवनवासपर्व","titleEn":"Arjunavanavasa Parva (Arjuna's forest exile)","verses":[{"text":"नारद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Narada said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो देवर्षयः सर्वे सिद्धाश्च परमर्षयः ।\nजग्मुस्तदा परामार्तिं दृष्ट्वा तत्कदनं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the divine sages, the siddhas and the supreme seers were sunk in deep distress at seeing that great slaughter."}},{"n":2,"text":"तेऽभिजग्मुर्जितक्रोधा जितात्मानो जितेन्द्रियाः ।\nपितामहस्य भवनं जगतः कृपया तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having mastered anger, themselves and their senses, they went in compassion for the world to the dwelling of the Grandfather."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततो ददृशुरासीनं सह देवैः पितामहम् ।\nसिद्धैर्ब्रह्मर्षिभिश्चैव समन्तात्परिवारितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There they saw the Grandfather seated with the gods, surrounded on every side by siddhas and Brahmin sages."}},{"n":4,"text":"तत्र देवो महादेवस्तत्राग्निर्वायुना सह ।\nचन्द्रादित्यौ च धर्मश्च परमेष्ठी तथा बुधः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were the god Mahadeva, Agni with Vayu, the moon and sun, Dharma, Parameshthin and Budha,"}},{"n":5,"text":"वैखानसा वालखिल्या वानप्रस्था मरीचिपाः ।\nअजाश्चैवाविमूढाश्च तेजोगर्भास्तपस्विनः ।\nऋषयः सर्व एवैते पितामहमुपासते ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Vaikhanasas, the Valakhilyas, the forest-dwellers, those who live on sunbeams, the Ajas and the Avimudhas, ascetics filled with radiance; all these sages attend the Grandfather."}},{"n":6,"text":"ततोऽभिगम्य सहिताः सर्व एव महर्षयः ।\nसुन्दोपसुन्दयोः कर्म सर्वमेव शशंसिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Coming together to him, all the great sages reported every deed of Sunda and Upasunda."}},{"n":7,"text":"यथाकृतं यथा चैव कृतं येन क्रमेण च ।\nन्यवेदयंस्ततः सर्वमखिलेन पितामहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"They told the Grandfather the whole of it, what had been done and how, and in what order."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततो देवगणाः सर्वे ते चैव परमर्षयः ।\nतमेवार्थं पुरस्कृत्य पितामहमचोदयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the hosts of gods and the supreme sages, putting that matter first, urged the Grandfather to act."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततः पितामहः श्रुत्वा सर्वेषां तद्वचस्तदा ।\nमुहूर्तमिव संचिन्त्य कर्तव्यस्य विनिश्चयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing all their words, the Grandfather reflected for a moment and decided what was to be done."}},{"n":10,"text":"तयोर्वधं समुद्दिश्य विश्वकर्माणमाह्वयत् ।\nदृष्ट्वा च विश्वकर्माणं व्यादिदेश पितामहः ।\nसृज्यतां प्रार्थनीयेह प्रमदेति महातपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the killing of the two in mind he summoned Vishvakarman, and on seeing him the great ascetic Grandfather commanded: Create here a woman to be desired."}},{"n":11,"text":"पितामहं नमस्कृत्य तद्वाक्यमभिनन्द्य च ।\nनिर्ममे योषितं दिव्यां चिन्तयित्वा प्रयत्नतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bowing to the Grandfather and welcoming his words, Vishvakarman thought carefully and fashioned a divine woman."}},{"n":12,"text":"त्रिषु लोकेषु यत्किंचिद्भूतं स्थावरजङ्गमम् ।\nसमानयद्दर्शनीयं तत्तद्यत्नात्ततस्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever beautiful thing there was in the three worlds, moving or unmoving, he carefully gathered from here and there."}},{"n":13,"text":"कोटिशश्चापि रत्नानि तस्या गात्रे न्यवेशयत् ।\nतां रत्नसंघातमयीमसृजद्देवरूपिणीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He set millions of jewels into her body, and so he made her, a goddess in form, as a mass of gems."}},{"n":14,"text":"सा प्रयत्नेन महता निर्मिता विश्वकर्मणा ।\nत्रिषु लोकेषु नारीणां रूपेणाप्रतिमाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Made with great effort by Vishvakarman, she was without equal in beauty among the women of the three worlds."}},{"n":15,"text":"न तस्याः सूक्ष्ममप्यस्ति यद्गात्रे रूपसंपदा ।\nन युक्तं यत्र वा दृष्टिर्न सज्जति निरीक्षताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There was not the smallest part of her body that lacked beauty or that the gaze, when it looked, did not cling to."}},{"n":16,"text":"सा विग्रहवतीव श्रीः कान्तरूपा वपुष्मती ।\nजहार सर्वभूतानां चक्षूंषि च मनांसि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"She was like Beauty herself in bodily form, lovely and shapely, and she captured the eyes and minds of all beings."}},{"n":17,"text":"तिलं तिलं समानीय रत्नानां यद्विनिर्मिता ।\nतिलोत्तमेत्यतस्तस्या नाम चक्रे पितामहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because she was made by gathering the jewels grain by grain, til by til, the Grandfather named her Tilottama."}},{"text":"पितामह उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The Grandfather said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"गच्छ सुन्दोपसुन्दाभ्यामसुराभ्यां तिलोत्तमे ।\nप्रार्थनीयेन रूपेण कुरु भद्रे प्रलोभनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Go, Tilottama, to the asuras Sunda and Upasunda, and with your desirable beauty lure them, auspicious one."}},{"n":19,"text":"त्वत्कृते दर्शनादेव रूपसंपत्कृतेन वै ।\nविरोधः स्याद्यथा ताभ्यामन्योन्येन तथा कुरु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Act so that, because of you, from the mere sight of your beauty, enmity arises between the two of them."}},{"text":"नारद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Narada said:"}},{"n":20,"text":"सा तथेति प्रतिज्ञाय नमस्कृत्य पितामहम् ।\nचकार मण्डलं तत्र विबुधानां प्रदक्षिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"She agreed, saying So be it, bowed to the Grandfather and made a circuit around the assembled gods."}},{"n":21,"text":"प्राङ्मुखो भगवानास्ते दक्षिणेन महेश्वरः ।\nदेवाश्चैवोत्तरेणासन्सर्वतस्त्वृषयोऽभवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The holy one sat facing east, Maheshvara to the south, the gods to the north, and the sages all around."}},{"n":22,"text":"कुर्वन्त्या तु तया तत्र मण्डलं तत्प्रदक्षिणम् ।\nइन्द्रः स्थाणुश्च भगवान्धैर्येण प्रत्यवस्थितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"As she made that circuit, Indra and the holy Sthanu stayed steady by firmness of mind."}},{"n":23,"text":"द्रष्टुकामस्य चात्यर्थं गतायाः पार्श्वतस्तदा ।\nअन्यदञ्चितपक्ष्मान्तं दक्षिणं निःसृतं मुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But when she passed at his side, Sthanu, greatly wishing to see her, grew another face to the south, its eyelashes curved."}},{"n":24,"text":"पृष्ठतः परिवर्तन्त्याः पश्चिमं निःसृतं मुखम् ।\nगतायाश्चोत्तरं पार्श्वमुत्तरं निःसृतं मुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As she turned behind him a western face appeared, and when she went to the north side a northern face appeared."}},{"n":25,"text":"महेन्द्रस्यापि नेत्राणां पार्श्वतः पृष्ठतोऽग्रतः ।\nरक्तान्तानां विशालानां सहस्रं सर्वतोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mahendra too grew a thousand wide, red-cornered eyes at the sides, behind and in front."}},{"n":26,"text":"एवं चतुर्मुखः स्थाणुर्महादेवोऽभवत्पुरा ।\nतथा सहस्रनेत्रश्च बभूव बलसूदनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this way Sthanu Mahadeva became four-faced, and the destroyer of Bala became thousand-eyed."}},{"n":27,"text":"तथा देवनिकायानामृषीणां चैव सर्वशः ।\nमुखान्यभिप्रवर्तन्ते येन याति तिलोत्तमा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise the faces of the hosts of gods and of the sages turned in every direction, whichever way Tilottama went."}},{"n":28,"text":"तस्या गात्रे निपतिता तेषां दृष्टिर्महात्मनाम् ।\nसर्वेषामेव भूयिष्ठमृते देवं पितामहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gaze of all those great-souled ones fell on her body, all except the god Grandfather."}},{"n":29,"text":"गच्छन्त्यास्तु तदा देवाः सर्वे च परमर्षयः ।\nकृतमित्येव तत्कार्यं मेनिरे रूपसंपदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"As she went, all the gods and supreme sages thought that their task was already done by her beauty."}},{"n":30,"text":"तिलोत्तमायां तु तदा गतायां लोकभावनः ।\nसर्वान्विसर्जयामास देवानृषिगणांश्च तान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Tilottama had gone, the Maker of the worlds dismissed all the gods and the hosts of sages."}}]}]}